# Dzen: RSS auto-import is ON — do NOT publish manually

The Dzen channel "Artem Dyachenko · Charter Capital"
(Studio editor id: `6a18826b19b0122c2924f370`) has an **RSS auto-import**
connected to `https://ccapital.pro/journal/feed.xml`.

Dzen pulls every new `<item>` from the feed automatically, with full
`content:encoded` body and the `<enclosure>` image as the cover. So once an
article is in `feed.xml` and deployed, **it will appear on Dzen on its own.**

## The duplicate trap (happened 2026-07-02)
Manually publishing an article that is ALSO in the feed creates **two copies**
on the channel (one manual, one RSS). We had 5 such duplicate pairs and cleaned
them up by keeping the RSS copy and deleting the manual one.

## Rule going forward
- **Do NOT manually publish journal articles to Dzen.** Just deploy the site
  (see `deploy.mdc`); the RSS import handles Dzen.
- Manual Dzen drafts under `drafts/dzen-*.md` are legacy — do not upload them
  unless the user explicitly asks.
- RSS copies are canonical: they carry the exact `feed.xml` title + hero cover.
- **Telegram is separate** — no auto-import there, so Telegram announcements
  are still posted manually as usual.

## If duplicates reappear
Audit via Dzen Studio publications list; same-title pairs are dupes. Keep the
RSS copy (title matches `feed.xml` verbatim), delete the other. Deletion in
Dzen is irreversible — confirm with the user first.
